WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.802
This example shows two versions of the same pivot
cell The first CASE

00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:11.731
has no ELSE zero so a missing Q3 response stays NULL
The second

00:00:11.758 --> 00:00:17.285
explicitly forces zero Run the query and find
respondents with

00:00:17.311 --> 00:00:22.868
no Q3 observation Ask whether zero is a real score
or

00:00:22.881 --> 00:00:28.609
simply a convenient placeholder That distinction
affects later averages

00:00:28.636 --> 00:00:29.294
and models
